---
const faqs = [
  { q: 'How long will the session last?', a: 'The workshop will be 3 hours long, packed with engaging and actionable insights.' },
  { q: 'What if I can\'t stay for the full session? Will I get a replay?', a: 'Yes! You will have access to the replay, along with all workshop resources, for one month after the event. You’ll also be able to ask any follow-up questions during that time.' },
  { q: 'Why can\'t I just get someone to manage my money for me? Must I do this myself?', a: 'There are two things you cannot outsource your health and your finances. You can hire a trainer, but only you can take the action and enjoy the results. The same applies to your career, no one can do it for you!' },
  { q: 'What makes this workshop different from other personal finance seminars?', a: 'This isn\’t just a lecture where you take notes. You’ll receive pre-session resources and actively work on your financial plan during the session. You\’ll leave with a personalised strategy and have partners available to help you take immediate action.' },
  { q: 'My money journey is unique. How do I know I\'ll get answers in this session?', a: 'Personal finance is indeed personal, but I guarantee you are not alone. Financial challenges are universal, and by using our workbook, you\’ll gain clarity through both information and introspection. With Oler\’s clear and confident teaching, you\’ll walk away with the knowledge you need to make smart investment decisions and build wealth, no matter the economic climate.' },
  { q: 'What do I walk away with?', a: 'A complete financial current state assessment, an inflation proofing framework, investment clarity, planning tools and templates, and expert answers to your specific financial situation from a live Q&A with Oler.' },
  { q: 'Is there a USD payment option?', a: 'Yes. Both NGN and USD checkout options are available when you join the waitlist.' },
  { q: 'What if I have never invested before?', a: 'Beat the Odds is designed to meet you where you are. Whether you are starting from scratch or restructuring an existing approach, the workshop gives you a framework and a plan built on your specific situation not a generic template.' },
]
---
<section class="py-20 md:py-28 px-6 bg-[#F9F8F5]">
  <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-black/50 mb-8">
        <span class="h-px w-6 bg-[#FFBD40]"></span>
        Frequently asked questions
      </div>
      <div class="space-y-2">
        {faqs.map((f, i) => (
          <div class="faq-item rounded-2xl border border-black/10 bg-white overflow-hidden">
            <button
              class="faq-trigger w-full flex items-center justify-between gap-4 px-6 py-5 text-left text-base font-semibold text-black hover:bg-black/5 transition"
              aria-expanded="false"
              data-index={i}
            >
              {f.q}
              <span class="faq-icon shrink-0 text-[#FFBD40] text-xl font-bold">+</span>
            </button>
            <div class="faq-content hidden px-6 pb-5 text-sm leading-relaxed text-black/60">
              {f.a}
            </div>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
      <div class="mt-10 text-center">
        <a href="#offer" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-full bg-[#FFBD40] px-6 py-3 text-sm font-bold text-black hover:brightness-95 transition">
          Join the Waitlist →
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<script is:inline>
  document.querySelectorAll('.faq-trigger').forEach((btn) => {
    btn.addEventListener('click', () => {
      const content = btn.nextElementSibling
      const icon = btn.querySelector('.faq-icon')
      const isOpen = btn.getAttribute('aria-expanded') === 'true'
      document.querySelectorAll('.faq-trigger').forEach((b) => {
        b.setAttribute('aria-expanded', 'false')
        b.nextElementSibling.classList.add('hidden')
        b.querySelector('.faq-icon').textContent = '+'
      })
      if (!isOpen) {
        btn.setAttribute('aria-expanded', 'true')
        content.classList.remove('hidden')
        icon.textContent = '×'
      }
    })
  })
</script>
